  "lineage": "Puerto Rican narrative-and-news song tradition originating in Ponce c. 1900 — built on the three sizes of pandereta frame drum (requinto small high-pitched lead, seguidor medium-pitched, segundo bass), plus voice and güiro scraper, performing topical-narrative songs about working-class urban Puerto Rican life and current events (the genres defining periódico cantado newspaper-set-to-music function); codified through Manuel Jiménez Canario (the first commercially-recorded plenero, 1925-onward), Mon Rivera (the mid-20th-century voice), and the modern Plena Libre, Los Pleneros de la 21, and Viento de Agua extensions",
